    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Corded Ware culture is named after the cord-like impressions on its pottery, and its other names, Single Grave and Battle Axe culture, come from its burials and its men's grave goods.</li><li>Ancient DNA shows its people shared much of their ancestry with the Yamnaya culture of the steppe, though whether they descended from the Yamnaya themselves is still argued.</li><li>It is considered a likely vector for the spread of many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-european-languages">Indo-European languages</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>About 3,000 battle axes have been found across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> in Battle Axe culture graves, and archaeologists think they were above all objects of status.</p></aside>
    </section>

